    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0957" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 342.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>General Sickles to Mr. Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 19.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Reply received to-night. Bases include numerous provisions. I send synopsis of
                    those inconsistent with your instructions.</p>
                <p>Both governments shall submit pending reclamations to arbitration in conformity
                    to following propositions:</p>
                <p>First. No indemnity for injuries resulting from judgment of civil or military
                    court or other judicial proceeding agreeably to Spanish law and procedure.</p>
                <p>Second. It must appear that the Spanish authorities inflicting the injury were
                    informed of the nationality of the claimant.</p>
                <p>Third. No right to indemnity if claim to American citizenship has been disallowed
                    by judgment of any Spanish civil or military tribunal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
